\h Psalm 151
\toc1 Psalm 151
\toc2 Psalm 151
\toc3 Ps2
\mt1 Psalm 151
\is1 Introduction
\ip \bk Psalm 151\bk* is a short additional song presented in David’s voice. He remembers being the youngest of his brothers, caring for his father’s sheep, and making music. Although his brothers were impressive in appearance, God chose him. The song ends by recalling his victory over Galyat (Goliath), the Pelishti (Philistine) who had challenged him.
\ip The song brings together events also found in 1 Samuel 16–17. Its emphasis is on God’s choice of an overlooked shepherd and the rescue accomplished through him. The title identifies it as a song beyond the usual collection of one hundred and fifty.
\ip \bk Psalm 151\bk* is recognised as Deuterocanonical Scripture by the Greek Orthodox and Russian Orthodox Churches.
\iot Main components of this song
\io1 David’s humble work and music \ior 1:1-3\ior*
\io1 God chooses David \ior 1:4-5\ior*
\io1 David defeats the Pelishti \ior 1:6-7\ior*
