\c 1
\cp 151
\s1 God chooses David and gives him victory
\d This Psalm is a genuine one of David, though extra,\f + \fr 1:0 \ft or, supernumerary\f* composed when he fought in single combat with Galyat.
\q1
\v 1 I was small among my brothers,
\q2 and the youngest in my father’s family.
\q2 I tended my father’s sheep.
\q1
\v 2 My hands made a musical instrument,
\q2 and my fingers tuned a lyre.
\q1
\v 3 Who’ll tell my master?
\q2 The master himself hears.
\q1
\v 4 He sent his messenger and took me from my father’s sheep,
\q2 and he anointed me with his anointing oil.
\q1
\v 5 My brothers were handsome and tall;
\q2 but the master didn’t take pleasure in them.
\q1
\v 6 I went out to meet the Pelishti,
\q2 and he cursed me by his idols.
\q1
\v 7 But I drew his own sword and beheaded him,
\q2 and removed the disgrace from the children of Yisrael \add (Israel)\add*.